>> title: Tripas
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, offal, mexican, griddle, tacos
>> counters: Taquería
>> aka: tripa, tripas, tripe, taco de tripas, tacos de tripa, tripitas, chinchulines
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas, salsa-verde
>> servings: 6
>> time: 3 hr
>> slack: unforgiving — it is all decided in the rinsing and the salt-and-vinegar rub, and nothing after the pot corrects what was left in

>> step: rinse, rub with salt and vinegar, rinse again
Rinse @beef small intestine{2%lb}(900 g; cleaned tripas) under cold running water, turning each length through, then rub it hard with @coarse salt{2%Tbs} and @white vinegar{1/4%cup}(60 mL) and rinse it again until the water runs clear.

>> step: simmer 2 hr in milk and water
Simmer @&(~1)cleaned tripas{} with @white onion{1/2}, @garlic{4%cloves}, @bay leaves{2}, @whole milk{2%cup}(475 mL), and @water{2%qt}(1.9 L) in a #stockpot{} for ~simmer{2%hr}, until a strand gives when you pinch it — the milk is what takes the barnyard off.

>> step: drain, cut in 3-in lengths, dry
Drain @&(~1)simmered tripas{}, cut them into 3-in lengths, and dry them well on a towel, because a wet strand steams instead of crisping.

>> step: crisp on the plancha 15 min
Crisp @&(~1)cut tripas{} on a hot #plancha{} in @lard{2%Tbs} with @kosher salt{1%tsp} for ~sear{15%min}, turning them, until the outside is hard and crackling and the inside is still chewy.
